01 - Network Design

1. Business scenario

A small branch office needs a single access switch that safely serves **staff** and **guest** users, is manageable only by an administrator, and is hardened against common Layer 2 attacks (rogue DHCP, ARP spoofing, MAC flooding, unauthorised devices, accidental loops).

 2. Requirements

| ID | Requirement |
|----|-------------|
| R1 | Separate staff and guest traffic into different VLANs |
| R2 | Provide automatic addressing (DHCP) for both user networks |
| R3 | Route between VLANs on the switch, with guests isolated from internal networks |
| R4 | Management only via SSHv2 from approved subnets; console for out-of-band access |
| R5 | Only one known device per access port; violations must be contained |
| R6 | Protect against rogue DHCP servers, ARP spoofing and accidental switching loops |
| R7 | Disable all unused ports |
| R8 | Fully documented, reproducible and tested |

