7. Security controls and rationale

| Control | Configuration | Threat mitigated |
|---------|---------------|------------------|
| VLAN segmentation | VLAN 10 / 20 / 99 | Lateral movement between user groups |
| Blackhole VLAN + shutdown | VLAN 999, unused ports `shutdown` | Unauthorised physical connection |
| Disable DTP | `switchport nonegotiate`, static access mode | VLAN hopping via trunk negotiation |
| Port security (sticky, max 1, shutdown) | Access ports | MAC flooding, device swapping |
| PortFast + BPDU guard | Access ports | Rogue switches, accidental loops |
| DHCP snooping + rate limit | VLAN 10, 20 | Rogue DHCP servers, DHCP starvation |
| Dynamic ARP Inspection | VLAN 10, 20 | ARP spoofing / poisoning |
| Storm control | Broadcast 20% on access ports | Broadcast storms |
| Guest ACL | `GUEST-IN` inbound on Vlan20 | Guest access to internal networks |
| SSH-only, ACL-restricted VTY | `MGMT-ACCESS`, `transport input ssh` | Unauthorised / cleartext management |
| Login throttling | `login block-for 120 attempts 3 within 60` | Brute-force logins |
| Errdisable auto-recovery | 300 s interval | Reduces admin overhead after violations |
| HTTP server disabled, banner, timeouts, encrypted passwords | Global / lines | Reduced attack surface |
| Root bridge priority 4096 | VLANs 10, 20, 99 | Deterministic STP root (future-proofs adding switches) |

8. Design decisions and limitations

- Switch is the DHCP server. DHCP snooping Option 82 insertion is disabled for this reason (see troubleshooting guide).
- DAI relies on the snooping binding table, so hosts must use DHCP. Static hosts would need ARP ACLs.
- Return traffic is blocked for guest to staff flows because the ACL is applied inbound on Vlan20 without stateful tracking; a Layer 3 switch has no stateful firewall. Guest isolation is therefore effectively bidirectional.
- Vlan99 uses no autostate so the management SVI stays up with no host in VLAN 99. If your IOS version rejects the command, the SVI comes up once a device is connected to Fa0/41-44.
- No uplink: Gi0/1-2 are shut down. A second switch or router would be required for STP topology changes, trunking and EtherChannel (see future work in the README).
